```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "list offers, or read one offer's field diff against canon"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///realm.offer.shows"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/realm.offer.shows"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/realm.offer.shows"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! realm.offer.shows ~ read the offer table

With no `cid`, the read lists the offers; with one, it answers that offer's field diff against canon. `bag` narrows to one bag; `all` lists every offer.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///realm.offer.shows", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ cid · bag · all · after · limit · nexus

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`cid` params=`takes/word seat/1 as/<cid> ~ the offer's content id; absent, every open offer`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/word ~ one bag`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`all` params=`~ every one`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`after` params=`takes/word ~ the cursor a prior page answered as next`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`limit` params=`takes/count ~ cap each surface's transcripts, oldest first`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`nexus` params=`takes/word ~ the Nexus whose offer table takes the row`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

